  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Am&#xe9;liorer la r&#xe9;ponse d&#x2019;&#xe9;ducation pour les enfants affect&#xe9;s par les violences dans la zone m&#xe9;tropolitaine de Port au Prince, D&#xe9;partement de l&#x2019;Ouest en R&#xe9;publique de Haiti</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide access and ensure sustained quality education to displaced children and children in host communities in the Port-au-Prince Metropolitan Area. This CEF project provides the establishment of 6 temporary classes and rehabilitation of 10 classrooms occupied by IDPs, with the provision of equipment including water points, latrines, and offices, distribution of school supplies to 1,000 children, kits to 60 teachers, and recreational kits among other activities. The project provides life-saving assistance to 1,125 people, including 50 women, 75 men, 1000 children, and 50 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
